-- Q12701: Federal Tax Procedures [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRM 8.6.1 and IRC Section 7803(e), the IRS Independent Office of Appeals settles cases based on the hazards of litigation — the probability the IRS would prevail in court. With only a 40% chance of winning, Appeals would likely offer a settlement conceding a significant portion of the $60,000 to reflect litigation risk.
Wrong (A): Appeals has broad authority under IRC Section 7122 to compromise disputes and is not limited to sustaining the full deficiency.
Wrong (B): Appeals does not dismiss cases based on probability thresholds; instead it settles by adjusting the amount to reflect the government''s litigation risk.
