  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Section 6664(c)(1), demonstrating reasonable cause and good faith reliance on a qualified CPA''s advice waives the accuracy-related penalty under Section 6662. Under IRC Section 6601(a), interest on underpayments accrues from the due date regardless of reasonable cause and generally cannot be abated on that basis.
Wrong (B): While the penalty is waived, interest continues to accrue because interest represents the time value of money owed to the government and is independent of fault or reasonable cause.
