-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under Circular 230, Section 10.50, the IRS Office of Professional Responsibility (OPR) may impose administrative sanctions including censure (a public reprimand), suspension, disbarment, and monetary penalties on practitioners who violate Circular 230 provisions.
Wrong (A): Criminal prosecution is handled by the Department of Justice, not the OPR. OPR sanctions are administrative, not criminal.
Wrong (B): CPA license revocation falls under state board of accountancy authority, not the IRS OPR, which governs only the right to practice before the IRS.
