-- Q13013: Professional Ethics in Tax [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under Circular 230 Section 10.30(a), practitioners are prohibited from soliciting employment through uninvited in-person contact with prospective clients. Torres''s unsolicited visit to the business owner''s office to offer representation violates this prohibition. Exceptions exist only for former clients and close family members.
Wrong (A): Providing a written engagement letter does not cure the solicitation violation; the prohibition applies to the uninvited in-person contact itself.
Wrong (C): An immediate need for representation does not create an exception to the solicitation prohibition under Circular 230.
Wrong (D): The fee amount is irrelevant; the prohibition is based on the method of solicitation, not the rate charged.$EXPL$
