-- Q13017: Professional Ethics in Tax [hard/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under Circular 230 Section 10.23, practitioners must act with due diligence and ensure prompt disposition of IRS matters, but this duty does not require overriding client decisions. Whitfield should advise the client about the consequences of signing or refusing the extension, then follow the client''s informed decision. The prompt disposition standard prohibits practitioner-caused delay, not client-directed strategy.
