Wrong (C): Signing without consulting the client violates the practitioner''s obligation to the client; Circular 230 does not require bypassing client authority.
Wrong (D): Withdrawal is unnecessary because the prompt disposition duty and client representation are not inherently in conflict when the client makes an informed choice.$EXPL$
